div.style:
width:64px; height:64px; border-radius:14px;
                                    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e3a5f 0%, #2d5a8e 100%);
                                    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(30,58,95,0.35);

div.div:
                                         nginx — Required for ADMS

                                        Add a dedicated /iclock/ block to prevent nginx sending
                                        an HTTP Date header that causes ZKteco firmware to
                                        sync the device clock and shift punch times.


                                        1. Install headers-more module:

                                        sudo apt install libnginx-mod-http-headers-more-filter
                                        2. Add before location / in your nginx site config:

                                        location /iclock/ {
  proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8069;
  proxy_http_version 1.1;
  proxy_set_header Host $host;
  proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
  proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
  proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
  proxy_redirect off;
  proxy_hide_header Date;
  more_clear_headers Date;
}
                                        3. Reload: sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx

                                        See SETUP.md for full documentation.

group.div:
                                             Custom Timezone (ADMS) —
                                            for branches outside your company's country.



                                            ⚠️ nginx Date Header Note:
                                            If your server runs behind nginx, the HTTP Date
                                            response header can cause some ZKteco firmware to drift the
                                            device clock. To prevent this, add this block to your nginx
                                            site config (requires libnginx-mod-http-headers-more-filter):


                                            location /iclock/ {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8069;
    proxy_hide_header Date;
    more_clear_headers Date;
}
                                            See SETUP.md for the full config.

div.t-attf-style:
height:4px; width:100%;
background: #{
    record.storage_warning.raw_value   ? '#f59e0b' :
    record.device_status.raw_value == 'online'  ? '#10b981' :
    record.device_status.raw_value == 'offline' ? '#ef4444' :
                                                  '#94a3b8'
};

